>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `lift_ssfrag`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.lift_ssfrag : simpLib.ssfrag -> simpExtLib.ssfrag
simpExtLib.lift_simpset : simpLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
simpExtLib.lift_simpset_without :
  string list -> simpLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Converts an ordinary fragment or simpset for the extension simplifier.

`lift_ssfrag frag` is an extension fragment with the rewrites,
conversions, decision procedures, congruence rules, AC rules and rewrite
filter of the `simpLib` fragment `frag`. Lifting the same named fragment
again gives the same result.

`lift_simpset ss` is an extension simpset built as `ss` was: its
fragments are lifted and added in the same order, and its deletions,
exclusions and limit are kept. A simpset that is extended over time, such
as `bossLib.srw_ss()`, must be lifted again to see the additions.

`lift_simpset_without names ss` is `lift_simpset ss` with the additions
of the fragments named in `names` left out; the deletions, exclusions and
limit of `ss` are kept, and a named fragment added to the result later is
not excluded.

There is no conversion in the other direction.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.++ (simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss,
     simpExtLib.lift_ssfrag boolSimps.DNF_ss);
>> simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV ss [] “p ∧ (q ∨ r)”;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.mk_simpset`](#simpExtLib.mk_simpset),
[`TraverseExt.CONFIG_REDUCER`](#TraverseExt.CONFIG_REDUCER).
